{
  "requirement": "The requirements index MUST show each requirement's evidence state as Valid, Missing, Determination false, FIXME, or Invalid. Valid MUST mean its determination is true and its record passes the same evidence and reference coverage checks as `habeas::validate()`. A false or FIXME determination MUST have its distinct state when the record passes all other checks. The FIXME state MUST pass validation while retaining its distinct label. Malformed or stale evidence MUST remain Invalid regardless of its determination. Each detail page MUST show any validation findings.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the implementation meets `requirements.index.state`, and the tests cover its main cases. I found no acknowledged gaps (no FIXME comments).\n\n**Implementation**\n\n- **State computation.** `LoadedDetailEvidence::load` (`src/index.rs`) takes the findings from the same `inspect_repository` report that backs `habeas::validate()`. It keeps the errors whose text starts with `evidence/<name>.json:`. That prefix covers every per-record check: schema, stale requirement text, stale inputs, definition dependencies, and uncovered `{impl}`/`{test}` references. It also covers the example-needs-a-test check and anchor coverage.\n- **State rules.** `load` then assigns the state as follows:\n  - **Missing:** the evidence file does not exist.\n  - **Valid / Determination false / FIXME:** there are no findings, and the state follows the parsed `Judgment` (true, false, or FIXME).\n  - **Determination false:** the only findings are the single \"determination is false\" finding.\n  - **Invalid:** any other findings, or a determination that cannot be parsed.\n  - A stale, malformed or uncovered record therefore stays Invalid whatever its determination.\n  - `validate_evidence_file` (`src/evidence.rs`) adds a finding only for a false determination, never for FIXME. FIXME therefore passes validation but keeps its own label.\n- **Labels.** `EvidenceState::label` produces exactly \"Valid\", \"Missing\", \"Determination false\", \"FIXME\" and \"Invalid\".\n- **Index table.** `DetailPlan::populate` builds the index table rows from `evidence.state().label()`.\n- **Detail pages.** `render_detail_sections` shows the state as a badge and renders a \"Validation findings\" section whenever there are findings. It does this for every determination, including false and FIXME.\n- **Shared use.** The same `load` is reused by `habeas status` and by authoring, so the state is computed one way throughout.\n- **Marking.** `load`, `state`, `errors`, `label`, `color`, `populate` and `render_detail_sections` carry `{impl}` for this requirement. The `EvidenceState` enum is marked `{cite}`, which the Rust coverage rule accepts.\n\n**Minor observations (not gaps)**\n\n- `color` assigns badge colours, which this requirement does not specify. It only supports the visual distinction of the states, so I did not treat it as an unspecified behaviour.\n- Findings that belong to no particular record are not folded into any record's state. Examples are Rust-function citation coverage, duplicate definitions and orphan files. They do not belong to a single record's evidence and reference checks, and they appear elsewhere (`status` \"Other validation findings\").\n\n**Tests**\n\n- `index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters` checks these states in the index table:\n  - Valid (the `ready` requirement).\n  - Determination false (`pending`).\n  - Invalid because the requirement text is stale (`changed`).\n  - Missing (`absent`).\n  - Invalid because an `{impl}` reference is uncovered while the determination is true (`uncovered`).\n  - It also checks the badge colour, the table alignment, and that the detail page shows the \"requirement text changed\" finding.\n- `findings_make_false_and_fixme_records_invalid` covers the boundary combinations:\n  - A clean false determination gives Determination false.\n  - A false determination that is stale, malformed or uncovered gives Invalid.\n  - A clean FIXME gives FIXME.\n  - A stale FIXME gives Invalid.\n  - Each page shows \"Validation findings\" except the clean FIXME page, which has none.\n- `tests/outcomes.rs` adds two failure cases through the shared load path:\n  - A malformed FIXME gives Invalid.\n  - A FIXME hit by a stale input or an uncovered reference gives Invalid and still shows its findings.\n  - It also checks that a valid FIXME shows \"FIXME\" in the index and on the detail page.\n- `index_and_detail_pages_show_each_example_evidence_state` repeats the state checks for examples.\n- A record with invalid JSON is not run through `load` in a test. The malformed-record fixtures use unexpected fields. `invalid_evidence_detail_remains_readable` renders the invalid-JSON page directly, so only the `load` classification of that case goes untested. This is a minor boundary.",
  "inputs": [
